#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"

I'd previously asked an agent:
> Write me a lua latex function that will lowercase and/or grey out all the matres lectiones in english transliterations like the middle column, and another that will do the same greying out and making smaller the matres in a hebrew column like the left. Then wrap these tables in that function without changing the positioning.

They're now in master.tex, and they're the functions \\trM and \\hJM.

They're currently taking a sort of shotgun approach and lowercasing letters that act as matres wherever they appear.

I want you to write a function \\hDefective{} and \\eDefective that actually have the knowledge required in order to make biblical hebrew words into plausibly real earlier defective spellings of those same words, and do the same for english transliterations thereof. Start with the words in the Pishon Gihon tables in 01-genesis/02.tex, in the crazy very after Verse 10 and before 11 that's a sort of modified Verse 11. For now, the implementation of \\hDefective and \\eDefective can be essentially a simple lookup table or a simple set of rules, but I want it to work for those tables in that file.
EOF
